WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.610 --> 00:00:12.670
In recent decades, it has been normal to consider
the tenant of the White House, the President

00:00:12.670 --> 00:00:19.280
of the United States, as the most powerful
person in the world.

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:32.410
However, dear viewer, things may be changing...
or may have already changed.

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:33.870
Have you heard about the Chinese President?

00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:38.309
Yes, of course you have, we mentioned him
several times here on VisualPolitik.

00:00:38.309 --> 00:00:43.390
See, Donald Trump himself, in statements collected
by the Washington Post, described the Chinese

00:00:43.390 --> 00:00:48.400
president, Xi Jinping, as the most powerful
leader that China has had in the last century...

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:53.149
which is as good as saying that Xi Jinping
is the most powerful Chinese leader of all

00:00:53.149 --> 00:00:54.329
time.

00:00:54.329 --> 00:01:00.270
So much so that more and more analysts are
wondering if he isn’t, in fact, the most

00:01:00.270 --> 00:01:02.880
powerful political leader in the world.

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:04.040
Yes, it’s true.

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:07.570
Both China's economy, as well as its army,
are still on a second level if we compare

00:01:07.570 --> 00:01:11.540
it to the United States... but, while Trump
seems to be consistently losing his influence

00:01:11.540 --> 00:01:18.780
over the world and, indeed, his own country,
the situation is quite the opposite for Xi

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:19.780
Jinping.

00:01:19.780 --> 00:01:20.780
Wait, wait, wait...

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:21.830
Trump is losing influence in the US?…

00:01:21.830 --> 00:01:31.210
How could this be if Donald wants to be everyone's
friend… have you seen his sweet tweets recently?

00:01:31.210 --> 00:01:36.190
Why would Kim Jong-un insult me by calling
me "old," when I would NEVER call him "short

00:01:36.190 --> 00:01:37.190
and fat?"

00:01:37.190 --> 00:01:40.720
Oh well, I try so hard to be his friend - and
maybe someday that will happen!

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:44.790
Yes... it's definitely no surprise that the
United States is losing its influence over

00:01:44.790 --> 00:01:45.790
the world...

00:01:45.790 --> 00:01:50.560
In very few months, Trump has gone from nuclear
war... to schoolyard fights.

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:52.140
Anyway, back to the serious stuff.

00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:56.030
The fact is that although Xi Jinping isn’t
the President of the world's leading power,

00:01:56.030 --> 00:02:00.890
he does control China’s leadership tightly,
a country which is one of the most important

00:02:00.890 --> 00:02:08.759
economic engines on the planet.

00:02:08.759 --> 00:02:13.880
And of course, for Beijing, Trump has been
something like… the Lottery Jackpot.

00:02:13.880 --> 00:02:20.420
Protectionism, nationalism, and Donald Trump’s
mistakes have allowed Xi Jinping, the President

00:02:20.420 --> 00:02:24.970
of China (the world's largest dictatorship)
to present his candidacy as a kind of global

00:02:24.970 --> 00:02:26.260
political leader.

00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:31.590
In January 2017, at the Davos Forum, Xi Jinping
promised that China would become nothing less

00:02:31.590 --> 00:02:37.099
than the champion of globalization, free trade,
and even the fight against climate change.

00:02:37.099 --> 00:02:41.070
Thus, Beijing aspires to put its grasp on
the terrain that Washington has been losing

00:02:41.070 --> 00:02:43.319
in international politics.

00:02:43.319 --> 00:02:56.700
He only forgot to mention freedom.. and you
know those sort of things…

00:02:56.700 --> 00:03:07.430
But what happened in the last Chinese Communist
Party Congress?

00:03:07.430 --> 00:03:09.489
How much power does Xi Jinping have?

00:03:09.489 --> 00:03:10.739
What does he want?

00:03:10.739 --> 00:03:23.150
Well, we’ll discuss this, but first let’s
take a look at China today.

00:03:23.150 --> 00:03:24.190
THE NEW CHINA

00:03:24.190 --> 00:03:30.780
Do you think that China is still that country
where people live under deplorable conditions,

00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:33.209
breaking their backs for miserable wages?

00:03:33.209 --> 00:03:34.209
Well...

00:03:34.209 --> 00:03:36.830
I'm sorry, but you're quite wrong.

00:03:36.830 --> 00:03:40.920
2018 will be the 40th anniversary of China's
reform and open policy.

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:44.560
And this country has changed a lot in that
time…

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:50.569
China is no longer a low-income country, but
a middle-income country.

00:03:50.569 --> 00:04:00.080
In fact, taking price differences into account,
it’d have purchasing power parity of about

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:05.879
$16,000, bigger than both Colombia and Brazil.

00:04:05.879 --> 00:04:14.040
Also, its economy has changed, and nowadays
services are the most important activity.

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:20.329
For example in electronic commerce, a sector
in which this country is beating Europe and

00:04:20.329 --> 00:04:27.710
even the United States, China represents no
less than 40% of all global transactions.

00:04:27.710 --> 00:04:31.210
The same can be said of mobile payments, which
are so popular in this country, that its market

00:04:31.210 --> 00:04:35.009
reached 5.5 trillion dollars in 2016.

00:04:35.009 --> 00:04:49.199
50 times more than the United States.

00:04:49.199 --> 00:04:50.580
Not bad, right?

00:04:50.580 --> 00:04:55.050
Their growth has been so large, that just
in the last 6 years, China’s private consumption

00:04:55.050 --> 00:05:00.520
has grown by 2.5 trillion dollars, an amount
that equals India’s entire GDP.

00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:05.699
Therefore, when visiting one of these big
Chinese cities, it isn’t odd to find a landscape

00:05:05.699 --> 00:05:09.520
full of skyscrapers, billionaires and high-speed
trains.

00:05:09.520 --> 00:05:15.219
But, wait a second… because China’s poverty
continues and, in general, there is a rather

00:05:15.219 --> 00:05:21.580
large difference between the country’s cities
and rural areas, which remain poor... &nbsp;very

00:05:21.580 --> 00:05:22.580
poor.

00:05:22.580 --> 00:05:29.649
So much so that 43 million people, almost
the entire population of Spain, still live

00:05:29.649 --> 00:05:33.619
in extreme poverty, earning less than $1 a
day.

00:05:33.619 --> 00:05:38.759
And not only that, almost 40% of Chinese people
still live at a fairly low economic level,

00:05:38.759 --> 00:05:43.339
although the situation is much better than
a few decades ago.

00:05:43.339 --> 00:05:49.509
This is all true, but as I said before, things
are changing very quickly, and we can no longer

00:05:49.509 --> 00:05:54.759
think of China as we did 20, 10 or even just
5 years ago.

00:05:54.759 --> 00:06:01.809
By the way, talking about poverty...

00:06:01.809 --> 00:06:06.249
here’s a interesting fact, do you know how
the Chinese government fights against poverty?

00:06:06.249 --> 00:06:11.229
Well, one of its main strategies is creating
new businesses and cooperatives in the poorest

00:06:11.229 --> 00:06:12.229
communities.

00:06:12.229 --> 00:06:16.699
To this end, the government has granted almost
400 billion dollars in small loans to help

00:06:16.699 --> 00:06:18.240
launch several companies.

00:06:18.240 --> 00:06:21.330
And, they not only focus on a money, but also
on culture.

00:06:21.330 --> 00:06:26.300
“The evening news is filled with tales of
rejuvenated communities, and villagers-turned-entrepreneurs

00:06:26.300 --> 00:06:30.719
heaping praise on Mr. Xi and the government
for providing loans and new apartments.”

00:06:30.719 --> 00:06:35.279
&nbsp;Javier C. Hernández, China correspondent
for The New York Times.

00:06:35.279 --> 00:06:38.550
Yes, I know...

00:06:38.550 --> 00:06:43.779
Xi Jinping and practically every country leader
talk a lot about "Chinese-style socialism"...

00:06:43.779 --> 00:06:48.360
The truth is, this is just a reference to
a kind of capitalist model locked within a

00:06:48.360 --> 00:06:49.360
dictatorship.

00:06:49.360 --> 00:06:52.129
China isn’t an ideological dictatorship...

00:06:52.129 --> 00:06:55.270
nor a socialist or communist one... it’s
simply a dictatorship.

00:06:55.270 --> 00:07:00.770
Having said this... let’s talk about Xi
Jinping, the person leading this new China,

00:07:00.770 --> 00:07:06.699
with almost complete power.

00:07:06.699 --> 00:07:12.020
XI JINPING, THE LEADER

00:07:12.020 --> 00:07:18.020
Born in 1953, we could say that Xi Jinping
is a pretty interesting guy.

00:07:18.020 --> 00:07:21.439
On the one hand, he’s probably the Chinese
leader who’s had the most contact with the

00:07:21.439 --> 00:07:22.439
West.

00:07:22.439 --> 00:07:26.580
His daughter studied at Harvard, his sister
lives in Canada, and he has visited the United

00:07:26.580 --> 00:07:27.879
States several times.

00:07:27.879 --> 00:07:32.499
In fact, in 2012 when he visited the United
States as vice president of China, he made

00:07:32.499 --> 00:07:35.229
a somewhat peculiar stop: he went to Iowa.

00:07:35.229 --> 00:07:36.899
“Iowa, why Iowa?”

00:07:36.899 --> 00:07:38.020
Obama wondered…

00:07:38.020 --> 00:07:43.080
Well, the fact is that in 1985 when Xi Jinping
was a young party county secretary in China,

00:07:43.080 --> 00:07:46.849
he traveled to Iowa to investigate agriculture-related
issues.

00:07:46.849 --> 00:07:51.439
So in 2012, he went to see the family he’d
stayed with at the time and brought them presents.

00:07:51.439 --> 00:07:52.839
Cool story, right?

00:07:52.839 --> 00:07:56.800
In addition, President Xi’s ‘Yankee’
side doesn’t end there, he’s also known

00:07:56.800 --> 00:07:58.969
to love Hollywood movies.

00:07:58.969 --> 00:08:03.020
But there’s also another side to this.

00:08:03.020 --> 00:08:06.990
Since he became China’s highest authority
5 years ago, his government has been characterized

00:08:06.990 --> 00:08:11.020
for having the most censorship and repression
for a very long time.

00:08:11.020 --> 00:08:14.979
We only need to take a look at the latest
cybersecurity law, which seeks to control

00:08:14.979 --> 00:08:18.759
even more Internet in China by restricting
anonymity.

00:08:18.759 --> 00:08:23.029
Indeed this is to such an extent that all
social network accounts have to be backed

00:08:23.029 --> 00:08:24.719
by an identified citizen.

00:08:24.719 --> 00:08:28.210
Further, it has been decades since China saw
such a strong a leader.

00:08:28.210 --> 00:08:30.339
We could say that propaganda has worked gradually.

00:08:30.339 --> 00:08:32.659
But… that’s not really surprising, is
it?

00:08:32.659 --> 00:08:40.890
The 
fact is that in these 5 years, Xi Jinping

00:08:40.890 --> 00:08:42.959
has made several changes in China...

00:08:42.959 --> 00:08:46.750
starting with the army reform and their very
active foreign policy.

00:08:46.750 --> 00:08:51.540
We saw it here, at VisualPolitik, how Xi Jinping
has diverted national resources towards foreign

00:08:51.540 --> 00:08:52.540
policy.

00:08:52.540 --> 00:08:56.950
A good example is the New Silk Road macro-project,
which aims to invest hundreds of billions

00:08:56.950 --> 00:08:58.759
of dollars in several countries.

00:08:58.759 --> 00:09:03.889
But generally, their greatest commitment has
definitely been the fight against corruption.

00:09:03.889 --> 00:09:06.540
And this is very important...

00:09:06.540 --> 00:09:11.360
Since Xi Jinping came to power, over one and
a half million members of the Communist Party

00:09:11.360 --> 00:09:17.230
have been sanctioned and nearly 300,000 have
been prosecuted, including 43 members of the

00:09:17.230 --> 00:09:18.230
Central Committee.

00:09:18.230 --> 00:09:19.250
And there’s more...

00:09:19.250 --> 00:09:23.490
Within the framework of this fight against
corruption, 13,000 army officers have been

00:09:23.490 --> 00:09:27.370
dismissed and more than 50 generals imprisoned.

00:09:27.370 --> 00:09:28.620
Of course...

00:09:28.620 --> 00:09:31.540
not everyone sees this battle as something
clean and honest:

00:09:31.540 --> 00:09:35.000
“It’s a selective anti-corruption campaign.

00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:37.730
Its nature is the selective protection of
corruption.

00:09:37.730 --> 00:09:41.019
When you purge some corrupt officials, you
are protecting the others.

00:09:41.019 --> 00:09:44.839
You protect the corrupt system, and you protect
corrupt people who support you.”

00:09:44.839 --> 00:09:46.600
Bao Tong, chinese activist.

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:51.830
Yes, Xi Jinping has mostly "relieved" his
political rivals, coincidence?!

00:09:51.830 --> 00:09:55.740
Of course, it’s very clear that Xi Jinping
has gained a lot of power in these five years.

00:09:55.740 --> 00:10:00.120
This was certainly observed in the last Chinese
Communist Party Congress, the most important

00:10:00.120 --> 00:10:05.240
political event in the country, which is held
every five years.

00:10:05.240 --> 00:10:10.510
THE 19TH CONGRESS

00:10:10.510 --> 00:10:19.529
This nineteenth Chinese Communist Party Congress,
held between October 18-24, 2017, was quite

00:10:19.529 --> 00:10:23.550
particular, especially because it may have
been the most austere Congress that the Chinese

00:10:23.550 --> 00:10:27.040
Communist Party has celebrated in many, many
years.

00:10:27.040 --> 00:10:30.329
On this occasion some amenities were removed,
want some examples?

00:10:30.329 --> 00:10:34.459
Well, among other things – and this is no
joke – the fancy buffet was abolished, as

00:10:34.459 --> 00:10:39.680
was hairdressing, facials and tailoring services,
which used to be offered for free to all participants

00:10:39.680 --> 00:10:41.520
and which had almost become a tradition.

00:10:41.520 --> 00:10:46.100
But above all, this was the Congress at which
Xi Jinping’s adoration reached its highest

00:10:46.100 --> 00:10:51.439
point, something that, as you can imagine
in China, means being put almost on a Mao-like

00:10:51.439 --> 00:10:52.670
level.

00:10:52.670 --> 00:10:57.459
“Five years ago I said he would be China’s
most powerful leader since Deng Xiaoping.

00:10:57.459 --> 00:10:58.459
I was wrong.

00:10:58.459 --> 00:11:03.750
He is now China’s most powerful leader since
Mao Zedong,” Kevin Rudd, Australia’s former

00:11:03.750 --> 00:11:04.750
Prime Minister.

00:11:04.750 --> 00:11:08.670
See, this Congress lead to the decision that
the so-called "Xi Jinping thought" should

00:11:08.670 --> 00:11:12.440
be included in the Communist Party Constitution.

00:11:12.440 --> 00:11:17.310
This may seem a bit strange, but it actually
means that Xi Jinping is no longer just another

00:11:17.310 --> 00:11:22.930
leader, he is THE leader, the leader whose
words form the party's own ideology.

00:11:22.930 --> 00:11:27.459
“It means Xi is effectively unassailable
… If you challenge Xi, you are challenging

00:11:27.459 --> 00:11:29.980
the party – and you never want to be against
the party.”

00:11:29.980 --> 00:11:32.610
Bill Bishop, publisher of the Sinocism newsletter.

00:11:32.610 --> 00:11:36.259
So far, only Mao Zedong had received such
an honor in life.

00:11:36.259 --> 00:11:37.259
But that's not all.

00:11:37.259 --> 00:11:40.829
Currently a president’s mandate is limited
to 10 years, which means that this would be

00:11:40.829 --> 00:11:45.650
Xi Jinping’s last term… but… wait a
minute… because no successor was considered

00:11:45.650 --> 00:11:53.389
during the congress, which leads us to believe
that Xi Jinping may be aspiring to, at least,

00:11:53.389 --> 00:11:56.029
a third mandate.

00:11:56.029 --> 00:12:01.520
“Chinese universities scramble to open centers
to study President Xi Jinping Thought”.

00:12:01.520 --> 00:12:05.970
But anyway, beyond the Chinese leader, this
Congress helped define 3 major priorities

00:12:05.970 --> 00:12:08.079
for the Chinese government for the upcoming
years:

00:12:08.079 --> 00:12:12.540
First - the Economy - fighting poverty and
opening up more to the world;

00:12:12.540 --> 00:12:15.620
Second - Launch an even stronger foreign policy

00:12:15.620 --> 00:12:18.360
Third - Start worrying about the Environment.

00:12:18.360 --> 00:12:25.459
And well, even though I said 3 priorities,
there is a fourth, and very clear one: consolidate

00:12:25.459 --> 00:12:28.930
the Communist Party’s power.

00:12:28.930 --> 00:12:32.550
Because, we know two things for sure:

00:12:32.550 --> 00:12:37.080
On the one hand, Xi Jinping and the Chinese
Communist Party will stay for a long time.

00:12:37.080 --> 00:12:40.519
And on the other, China will reclaim its role
as a superpower.

00:12:40.519 --> 00:12:44.540
So let’s get used to taking Beijing into
account...

00:12:44.540 --> 00:12:45.699
Now it's your turn.

00:12:45.699 --> 00:12:50.920
Who do you think will leave power first, XI
Jinping or Vladimir Putin?!

00:12:50.920 --> 00:12:54.201
Leave your answer in the comments as well
as in the survey.

